---
title: RTC - real-time clock
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY. No signal pins to wire.
%% The 32.768 kHz crystal on PC14/PC15 is already fitted on the DISC1.
%% VBAT is tied to VDD on this board unless you cut the solder bridge, so the
%% clock and the backup registers do NOT survive a power cut as shipped.
%% Choose LSE for real timekeeping; LSI drifts far too much for a clock.
flowchart LR
    subgraph XTAL["On-board crystal"]
        OSCIN["PC14 - OSC32_IN"]
        OSCOUT["PC15 - OSC32_OUT"]
        Q["32.768 kHz crystal"]
    end

    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1 - backup domain"]
        LSE["LSE oscillator - accurate"]
        LSI["LSI ~32 kHz - drifts"]
        PRE["Async /128 + sync /256 prescalers"]
        CAL["Calendar - date and time BCD"]
        ALRM["Alarm A / Alarm B"]
        BKPR["20 backup registers"]
        WK["Wake from Standby"]
    end

    subgraph PWRIN["Backup supply"]
        VBAT["VBAT pin - tied to VDD on this board"]
        COIN["Optional coin cell if the bridge is cut"]
    end

    Q --- OSCIN
    Q --- OSCOUT
    OSCIN --> LSE
    LSE --> PRE
    LSI -.-> PRE
    PRE --> CAL
    CAL --> ALRM
    ALRM --> WK
    BKPR --- VBAT
    CAL ---|"backup supply"| VBAT
    COIN -.-> VBAT
